    "seo": {
      "title": "Complete Your Onboarding",
      "description": "Securely complete your employee onboarding details from the link your HR team emailed you."
    },
    "navigation": {
      "showHeader": true,
      "showFooter": true
    },
    "kind": "external",
    "pageMode": "web",
    "beforeLoad": {
      "enabled": true,
      "mode": "business_logic",
      "business_logic": {
        "method": "seed_access_key",
        "language": "plpgsql",
        "description": "Read the onboarding key from the URL and pre-populate the form with the candidate's on-file details for that key",
        "spec": "On page load, read the candidate key from the page URL params (accept either ?key= or ?access_key=), trim it, and always return it via set_vars as access_key so the key-validation gate and API loaders can run. Do not deny access here (always return allowed=true); key validity, expiry and already-submitted checks are handled by the client-side validate-key API gate, which also renders the form only when the key is valid. If no key is present, return access_key as an empty string and set no other vars. When a non-empty key is present, look up the single emponb_candidate_record row whose ACCESS_KEY equals that trimmed key; if a matching candidate is found, additionally return via set_vars that candidate's identity and on-file onboarding details so the form is pre-filled with whatever has already been captured for this candidate_id (HR-captured values on first open, plus any previously saved values on a return visit). Map each candidate_record column to the matching page input variable of the same lowercased name: candidate_id (CANDIDATE_ID), candidate_name (CANDIDATE_NAME), name_prefix (NAME_PREFIX), emp_fname (EMP_FNAME), emp_mname (EMP_MNAME), emp_lname (EMP_LNAME), gender (GENDER), birthdate (BIRTHDATE), nationality (NATIONALITY), marital_status (MARITAL_STATUS), marriage_anniversary (MARRIAGE_ANNIVERSARY), blood_group (BLOOD_GROUP), religion (RELIGION), cast_category (CAST_CATEGORY), mother_tongue (MOTHER_TONGUE), physical_handicap (PHYSICAL_HANDICAP), hobby1 (HOBBY1), hobby2 (HOBBY2), total_experience (TOTAL_EXPERIENCE), current_address (CURRENT_ADDRESS), current_pin (CURRENT_PIN), current_city (CURRENT_CITY), current_state (CURRENT_STATE), permanent_address (PERMANENT_ADDRESS), permanent_pin (PERMANENT_PIN), permanent_city (PERMANENT_CITY), permanent_state (PERMANENT_STATE), mobile (MOBILE), alternate_telephone (ALTERNATE_TELEPHONE), contact_person (CONTACT_PERSON), contact_person_mobile (CONTACT_PERSON_MOBILE), contact_person_email (CONTACT_PERSON_EMAIL), pan_no (PAN_NO), aadhar_no (AADHAR_NO), passport_no (PASSPORT_NO), driving_lic_no (DRIVING_LIC_NO), pf_no (PF_NO), esic_no (ESIC_NO), bank_account_no (BANK_ACCOUNT_NO), bank_ifsc_code (BANK_IFSC_CODE), bank_name (BANK_NAME). Dates should be returned as ISO yyyy-mm-dd strings and NULL columns omitted or returned as empty so they do not overwrite anything. Always include access_key in set_vars. If no candidate row matches the key, return only access_key (still allowed=true) so the invalid-link callout can show."
      }
    },
    "blocks": []
  }
